From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 04:20:00 +0200
Subject: net: stmmac: stop PHY polling while the MAC waits for a magic packet

With MAC wake-up phylink_suspend() leaves the PHY state machine
running. On ROCK Pi 4A (RK3399, RTL8211E without interrupt) the
machine polls the PHY over MDIO every second, and a poll that lands
after dwmac1000_pmt() makes the MAC miss the magic packet: s2idle
wake-up failed in about 40 % of suspends, each failure with such a
poll (17 of 17).

Cancel the state machine work before programming PMT and start it
again after phylink_resume(). With this, 20 of 20 suspends woke on the
magic packet and no trace showed an MDIO poll between PMT and resume.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -8212,6 +8212,10 @@ int stmmac_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	if (!ndev || !netif_running(ndev))
 		goto suspend_bsp;

+	/* With MAC wake-up an MDIO poll after PMT makes the MAC miss the magic packet */
+	if (priv->wolopts && ndev->phydev)
+		cancel_delayed_work_sync(&ndev->phydev->state_queue);
+
 	mutex_lock(&priv->lock);

 	netif_device_detach(ndev);
@@ -8408,6 +8412,9 @@ int stmmac_resume(struct device *dev)
 	phylink_resume(priv->phylink);
 	rtnl_unlock();

+	if (priv->wolopts && ndev->phydev)
+		phy_start_machine(ndev->phydev);
+
 	netif_device_attach(ndev);

 	ret = 0;
